  "details": "Being someone with a visual impairment, I feel like it would really benefit a lot of people if these features were implemented.\n\nText box TTS- having Texas speech go off when a text box appears would be highly beneficial. I’m not sure how it would work with how close or far you are to someone, but in the sense of who can hear text to speech, it would be great if it was just a toggle. That way those of us who don’t want text to speech could have it disabled, but for people with heavy visual impairments, they could enable it and still be able to know what a mute person is saying in their speech box. As for if you have people blocked, it would be great if when you block or mute people, it would also block or mute their text box.\n\nResizable camera- time and time again I have found myself really struggling to use the camera in VR because of how small the buttons are. It would be cool to have an option to resize the camera or have extra large buttons somehow. Maybe there could be a separate panel that has large buttons with text descriptions that could control the camera like the regular buttons do. This feature could be useful if it was behind a toggle. As I know, a lot of people don’t need to resize the camera. It would be great for those who do to be able to enable a larger camera and buttons.",
